-- title:
--   Admissible constants over a cyclotomic discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes, let $L$ be a characteristic-zero field which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for the set $\{q\ell\}$, let $\xi\in L$ be a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its fraction field and with $q$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$. Then there exist a valuation subring $\bar A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $\bar A$, an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to k_0$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $\bar A$, such that, writing $A_0:=\bar A\cap k_0$ for the preimage of $\bar A$ under $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, $A_0$ is a henselian local ring, the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed, and every $a\in\bar A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $\bar A$ to some $c\in k_0$ with $c\in\bar A$; moreover $\iota$ carries the image of $A$ in $L$ into $\bar A$, and conversely any $x\in L$ with $\iota(x)\in\bar A$ comes from $A$; and there is a ring homomorphism $\iota_{\mathbb{C}}\colon k_0\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota_{\mathbb{C}}(\iota(\xi))=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$.
--
--   This is the extension-of-valuations step (Chevalley extension to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by passage to the fixed field of the inertia subgroup) that produces the base data — a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, containing a chosen copy of the $q\ell$-th cyclotomic field with prescribed complex embedding of $\xi$ — for the analysis of the semistable fibre at $q$ of the modular curve of full level. It is invoked by the `AuxLevelOne` lemmas on the two-chart integral model and its associated $j$-sets.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_valuationSubring_admissibleConstants_over_cyclotomic.lean

